<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#dictatorship">Glossary</a> · Term · government</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dictatorship</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 501 BCE – present</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dictatorship began as a lawful Roman office, supreme power granted for a single emergency and surrendered when it passed. In the modern world the word came to mean rule without legal limits or free elections, by soldiers, single parties or one man; it was the form under which many of the 20th century’s mass killings took place, and it remains common today.</p></div>
